    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "category": "questioning_technique",
      "evidence": "The interviewer repeatedly asked the same GAD-7 questions multiple times when the patient expressed confusion, rather than finding a more efficient way to clarify the scale once the patient's difficulty was established."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "flow",
      "evidence": "In the 'current_concerns' section, the interviewer asked 'What specifically happens during those days—for example, do you feel low or anxious, have trouble sleeping, or struggle to concentrate?' after the patient had already provided some of this information, leading to a slightly redundant flow."
